wajo22_q5.solution:
Let the distance Mark travelled be $x \mathrm{~km}$. Then<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
4631+x &amp; =10(173.3+x) \\
&amp; =1733+10 x \\
9 x &amp; =4631-1733 \\
&amp; =2898 \\
x &amp; =322 \mathrm{~km}
\end{aligned}
$$<br>So Mark travelled 322 km, at which time the readings were:<br> \begin{gather*} \text{odometer:} 4953 \\ 
 \text{tripmeter:} 495.3 \end{gather*}

wajo22_q11.solution:
Let $R$ be the radius of the roll. Then, the cross-sectional area of the roll is,<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
\pi R^{2} &amp; =\text{ tube_cross-sectional_area }+ \text{ rolled_copper_cross-sectional_area } \\
&amp; =\pi(10 / 2 \mathrm{~cm})^{2}+1710 \pi \mathrm{~cm} \cdot 1 \mathrm{~mm} \\
&amp; =(25 \pi+171 \pi) \mathrm{cm}^{2} \\
&amp; =196 \pi \mathrm{~cm}^{2} \\
\therefore R &amp; =14 \mathrm{~cm}
\end{aligned}
$$<br>So the diameter of the roll is $2 R=2 \times 14=28 \mathrm{~cm}$.
